This paper delves into the characteristics of entire functions $f$ where the differences between $f$ and $A$ are sparse within a certain growth category. It is demonstrated that under specific conditions regarding the exponent of convergence for the periodic singularities of $B = f + A$, the periodic function $A$ must be constant, leading to $B$ being equivalent to $2^{
u}f$. Consequently, this implies that $m_r(2^{
u}f) \sim 2 m_r(f)$, where $0 \le 
u < 1$.
